# DevFlow Core

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md). When CodeBuddy supports skills, load `skills/devflow-core/SKILL.md` and its shared methods source; Core then loads only the selected lifecycle reference. Without skills, use the portable fallback in `AGENTS.md`.

Preserve Core routing for non-unique artifacts, explicit STOP gates, selective memory recall, direct independent-review routes, and Prove before completion. Core's risk gate may send a clear local reversible existing-feature change with one plausible path, no security/data-loss/permission/contract risk, and quick proof directly to Cut; ambiguous or materially risky creative work starts `devflow-brainstorm`. Cut and Prove remain required. User-selected A/B/C success edges proceed directly and all other artifacts return Core. This adapter does not restate skill internals.

Apply independent judgment: check false premises, logical leaps, and material missing information; distinguish facts, inferences, and opinions; verify material claims when practical; state evidence boundaries, risks, alternative explanations, and overlooked variables instead of agreeing by default.
